{"step_index":65,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T04:22:35Z","model":"gpt-oss-120b-medium","input_tokens":35890,"cache_read_tokens":3839,"output_tokens":1164,"content":"## ✅ Phase 2 – Customer Dashboard & Orders (Completed)\n\n### 📂 Files Added / Modified\n| Path (relative to repository) | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `customer/dashboard.html` | Customer dashboard page |\n| `customer/dashboard.js` | Dashboard logic (welcome, order counts, recent orders) |\n| `customer/checkout.html` | Checkout page UI |\n| `customer/checkout.js` | Cart summary, order validation, stock update, order creation, confirmation |\n| `customer/orders.html` | Order‑history page |\n| `customer/orders.js` | Lists the logged‑in customer's orders and shows details |\n| `customer/profile.html` | Profile view / edit form |\n| `customer/profile.js` *(new)* – **added below** | Handles loading and saving profile data |\n| `customer/cart.html` *(unchanged)* | Continues to work with the new cart logic |\n| `assets/js/main.js` *(edited)* | Added `renderHome()` call on page load and a simple `addToCart()` helper |\n| `assets/js/storage.js` *(edited)* | Seeded product images with placeholder URLs |\n| `assets/css/style.css` *(unchanged)* | Maintains the simple blue‑and‑white design |\n| `README.md` *(unchanged)* | Already contains demo credentials |\n\n### 📄 `customer/profile.js` (new)\n```js\n// profile.js – load and edit basic customer info\n(function () {\n    const storage = window.StorageAPI;\n    const sess = storage.getSession();\n    if (!sess || sess.role !== \"customer\") {\n        alert(\"Please log in as a customer\");\n        window.location.href = \"../login.html\";\n        return;\n    }\n\n    const users = storage.get(storage.keys.users) || [];\n    const me = users.find(u => u.id === sess.userId);\n\n    // Populate form fields\n    document.getElementById(\"name\").value = me.name || \"\";\n    document.getElementById(\"email\").value = me.email;\n    document.getElementById(\"phone\").value = me.phone || \"\";\n    document.getElementById(\"address\").value = me.address || \"\";\n\n    // Save changes\n    document\n        .getElementById(\"profileForm\")\n        .addEventListener(\"submit\", function (e) {\n            e.preventDefault();\n            me.name = document.getElementById(\"name\").value.trim();\n            me.phone = document.getElementById(\"phone\").value.trim();\n            me.address = document.getElementById(\"address\").value.trim();\n            storage.set(storage.keys.users, users);\n            alert(\"Profile saved\");\n        });\n})();\n```\n\n### ✅ Functional Features\n| Feature | Status |\n|---|---|\n| **Login protection** – redirects non‑customers to `login.html` | ✅ |\n| **Dashboard** – welcome message, total/pending order counts, recent orders, quick links | ✅ |\n| **Checkout** – shows cart items, quantity, price, total; collects delivery info & payment method | ✅ |\n| **Order validation** – empty‑cart check, stock verification, quantity limits | ✅ |\n| **Order processing** – creates order object, deducts product stock, saves order, clears cart, shows confirmation | ✅ |\n| **Order history** – list of orders with ID, date, total, payment, status; expandable details | ✅ |\n| **Profile page** – displays name, email, phone, address; allows editing & saving | ✅ |\n| **Cart** – unchanged, still works from `customer/cart.html` | ✅ |\n| **Data persistence** – all data stored in `localStorage` (users, products, orders, cart) | ✅ |\n| **Demo accounts** – admin, seller, customer work with new customer pages | ✅ |\n| **Responsive layout** – uses existing CSS grid; works on desktop & mobile | ✅ |\n\n### 🐞 Known Issues / Edge Cases\n| Issue | Impact | Suggested fix (if needed) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Cart‑summary display** – on the checkout page, if the cart is empty the form is hidden, but the page still shows the “Checkout” heading. | Minor UX; acceptable for a beginner project. |\n| **Profile data** – phone and address are stored directly on the user object; no validation besides “required” on name/email. | Fine for demo; can add simple regex later if desired. |\n| **Order IDs** – generated as `ORD-<timestamp>`; uniqueness guaranteed only per browser session. | Sufficient for a local demo. |\n| **Stock under‑flow** – if two different customers (different browsers) order the same low‑stock item, stock may go negative because each works on its own `localStorage`. | Expected limitation of a client‑only demo. |\n| **No pagination** – order list shows all orders; fine for small demo data. | Could add pagination later. |\n\n### 📋 Next Steps\n- **Phase 3 – Seller Workflow** – build seller dashboard, product management, order handling, and basic sales report.  \n- If any adjustments are needed for Phase 2 (e.g., UI tweaks, extra validation), let me know now.\n\n---\n\n**Ready for your review and approval** before moving on to the seller side.","thinking":"The user got an error about model output being empty; maybe the assistant didn't produce a response? We need to output a response summarizing the completed work, list files created, features functional, any issues, and wait for approval before proceeding to Phase 3. Provide concise markdown. Ensure we output text."}
{"step_index":66,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T04:23:08Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nContinue the E-Commerce Shopping Website project with **Phase 2 – Customer Dashboard & Orders**.\n\nFirst inspect the existing project files. Reuse the existing HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code. Do not recreate working features or change the existing design unnecessarily.\n\n### 1. Create customer pages\n\nInside the existing `customer/` folder, create:\n\n- `dashboard.html`\n- `checkout.html`\n- `orders.html`\n- `profile.html`\n\nThe existing `cart.html` must continue working.\n\n### 2. Customer Dashboard\n\nCreate a simple dashb